    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nneovim when used inside kmscon doesn't change cursror shape based on change of mode, while kmscon itself does support DECSCUSR escape sequences already.\n\nSee: https://github.com/kmscon/kmscon/issues/565\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* Open neovim in kmscon\n* Set guicursor like this:\n\n```lua\n:lua vim.o.guicursor = 'n-v-c:block,i-ci-ve:ver25,r-cr:hor20,o:hor50,' .. 'a:blinkwait700-blinkoff400-blinkon250-Cursor/lCursor,' .. 'sm:block-blinkwait175-blinkoff150-blinkon175'\n```\n\n* Enter insert mode with I and note how cursor shape doesn't change from block to vertical bar\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nCursor shapes should change.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.6\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\n---\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nDebian testing Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkmscon 10.0.4\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nkmscon\n\n### Installation\n\nappimage",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
