            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Regarding system terminfo for kmscon, that's what I see, but not sure how to interpret that in regards to what cursor capabilities neovim derives from it:\n\n```\ninfocmp kmscon\n#       Reconstructed via infocmp from file: /usr/share/terminfo/k/kmscon\nkmscon|KMS Console,\n        am, bce, km, mir, msgr, npc, xenl,\n        colors#0x100, cols#80, lines#24, pairs#0x7fff,\n        acsc=``aaffggiijjkkllmmnnooppqqrrssttuuvvwwxxyyzz{{||}}~~,\n        bel=^G, bold=\\E[1m, cbt=\\E[Z, civis=\\E[?25l,\n        clear=\\E[H\\E[2J, cnorm=\\E[?25h, cr=\\r,\n        csr=\\E[%i%p1%d;%p2%dr, cub=\\E[%p1%dD, cub1=^H,\n        cud=\\E[%p1%dB, cud1=\\n, cuf=\\E[%p1%dC, cuf1=\\E[C,\n        cup=\\E[%i%p1%d;%p2%dH, cuu=\\E[%p1%dA, cuu1=\\E[A,\n        dch=\\E[%p1%dP, dch1=\\E[P, dl=\\E[%p1%dM, dl1=\\E[M,\n        ech=\\E[%p1%dX, ed=\\E[J, el=\\E[K, el1=\\E[1K,\n        flash=\\E[?5h$<200/>\\E[?5l, home=\\E[H, hpa=\\E[%i%p1%dG,\n        ht=^I, hts=\\EH, ich=\\E[%p1%d@, ich1=\\E[@, il=\\E[%p1%dL,\n        il1=\\E[L, ind=\\n, indn=\\E[%p1%dS, kLFT=\\E[1;2D,\n        kRIT=\\E[1;2C, kbs=^?, kcbt=\\E[Z, kcub1=\\E[D, kcud1=\\E[B,\n        kcuf1=\\E[C, kcuu1=\\E[A, kdch1=\\E[3~, kend=\\E[F, kf1=\\EOP,\n        kf10=\\E[21~, kf11=\\E[23~, kf12=\\E[24~, kf13=\\E[25~,\n        kf14=\\E[26~, kf15=\\E[28~, kf16=\\E[29~, kf17=\\E[31~,\n        kf18=\\E[32~, kf19=\\E[33~, kf2=\\EOQ, kf20=\\E[34~,\n        kf21=\\E[23;2~, kf22=\\E[24;2~, kf3=\\EOR, kf4=\\EOS,\n        kf5=\\E[15~, kf6=\\E[17~, kf7=\\E[18~, kf8=\\E[19~, kf9=\\E[20~,\n        khome=\\E[H, kich1=\\E[2~, kmous=\\E[M, knp=\\E[6~, kpp=\\E[5~,\n        op=\\E[39;49m, rc=\\E8, rep=%p1%c\\E[%p2%{1}%-%db,\n        rev=\\E[7m, ri=\\EM, rin=\\E[%p1%dT, rmacs=\\E(B,\n        rmcup=\\E[?1049l, rmso=\\E[27m, rmul=\\E[24m, rs2=\\Ec, sc=\\E7,\n        setab=\\E[%?%p1%'\\010'%<%t4%p1%d%e%p1%'\\020'%<%t10%p1%'\\010'%-%d%e48;5;%p1%d%;m,\n        setaf=\\E[%?%p1%'\\010'%<%t3%p1%d%e%p1%'\\020'%<%t9%p1%'\\010'%-%d%e38;5;%p1%d%;m,\n     