        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Hmm, digging around, here is one idea:\n\n**for konsole:**\n```\ninfocmp -x konsole | rg 'Ss|Se|civis|cnorm|cvvis'\n        bel=^G, blink=\\E[5m, bold=\\E[1m, civis=\\E[?25l,\n        clear=\\E[H\\E[2J, cnorm=\\E[?25h, cr=\\r,\n        PE=\\E[201~, PS=\\E[200~, RV=\\E[>c, Rmol=\\E[55m, Se=\\E[0 q,\n        Smol=\\E[53m, Smulx=\\E[4:%p1%dm, Ss=\\E[%p1%d q,\n```\n\n**for kmscon:**\n```\ninfocmp -x kmscon | rg 'Ss|Se|civis|cnorm|cvvis'\n        bel=^G, bold=\\E[1m, cbt=\\E[Z, civis=\\E[?25l,\n        clear=\\E[H\\E[2J, cnorm=\\E[?25h, cr=\\r,\n```\n\n@justinmk: So looks like terminfo for kmscon is missing some of the DECSCUSR details (may be neovim relies on that?). I think the relevant ones are `Ss` and `Se`:\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/src/gen/terminfo.lua#L72-L73\n\nI can ping kmscon developers about it if you think that could help.",
